    "translationNote": "`naam`, `hoofdfunctieNaam` and `omschrijvingIv3` are the STATUTORY Dutch strings and are what a CBS Iv3 submission carries. They are identifiers, not display text, and must never be replaced by a translation. The `*En` fields alongside them are display-only, for an English UI locale. If the two ever disagree, the Dutch one is right by definition. Entries with no `omschrijvingIv3` in the source regulation carry no `omschrijvingIv3En` either — an absent description is not translated into an invented one."
